      "updated_at": "2018-11-17T12:59:55Z",
      "body": "**Comment from Joseph Banks:**\n\nI don't know if I like the idea of this. I'd like to see the opinions of others. Most of what we display in the public user command is collected at the time of execution of this command. I like it this way because we aren't storing too much data about our users, which I believe in. I think that storing this kind of information, and even displaying it to other users is a breach of users privacy and might not be what we are going for. This would be collecting data which isn't related to our guild, this is the user coming online.\n\nI could *maybe* back some sort of last message time being stored but I don't think that storing the users status is something which I would be invested in at this time.",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
